# The manual's invented hardware keys (#2314) — the PUBLIC halves only, generated once and fixed.
#
# Six self-signed certificates belonging to no real device: all six 5-series models, two people carrying two
# keys each, each certificate carrying its holder's address in the subject alternative name (so the tenant's
# strict binding resolves its holder) and a ten-year validity from the manual's frozen demo clock
# (2026-06-01 → 2036-06-30). The private keys were discarded at generation: the capture enrols these and
# seals TO them; nothing ever opens the document.
#
# Fixed on purpose. A certificate minted per capture run would change its subject key identifier and its
# serial — both of which the seal inspection prints — and the two figures would churn on every manual
# regeneration. The order below MUST match SealedAudienceFixture.Keys.

